   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p><span><a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2HG6kt9w0nxryQZhCV4uTy\">Microsoft R Open</a></span><span> 3.2.3, the enhanced open source R distribution from Microsoft, is now <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/download/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/download/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TjdnAxT8IZ0XmJJbtIdoN\"><span>available for download.</span></a> <b>Revolution R Open is now known as Microsoft R Open (MRO). </b></span></p><p><span><br></span></p><p><span>This update brings <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/multithread/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/multithread/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3jnMbY28e1uWg9jCdnrHS8\"><span>multi-threaded performance</span></a> to the latest update to the R engine from the <a href=\"https://www.r-project.org/contributors.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.r-project.org/contributors.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0e_VvI1u-8qGmyskXx9S2J\"><span>R Core Group</span></a>, which includes <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/news/#r323\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/news/%23r323&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1di8XToe5bxfWd_sYVLSx9\"><span>several improvements and bug fixes</span></a>. Significant amongst these is default support for HTTPS connections, making it easy to follow the <a href=\"http://blog.revolutionanalytics.com/2015/08/good-advice-for-security-with-r.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blog.revolutionanalytics.com/2015/08/good-advice-for-security-with-r.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bzD4yU23yfO1pajVhcrvk\"><span>best practices for R security</span></a> recommended by the R Consortium. The <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/reproducibility/#timemachine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/reproducibility/%23timemachine&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TfMb1OKb1bXSJsFmZZ4Ew\"><span>checkpoint package</span></a> included with Microsoft R Open likewise uses HTTPS when downloading R package versions for reproducible data analysis.</span></p>\r\n<p><span></span><br></p>\r\n<p><span>MRO 3.2.3 is available for download now for<a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/installation/#sysreq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/installation/%23sysreq&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JKxePMeasU7eoR6D7XEW7\"><span> Windows, Mac and Linux systems</span></a>, and is <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/#compatible\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/%23compatible&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mz2eOji4EfG_mK1cHdckV\"><span>100% compatible</span></a> with R 3.2.3.</span></p>\r\n<p><span></span><br></p>\r\n<p><span>You can download Microsoft R Open now from the link below, and we welcome comments, suggestions and other discussion on this forum.  If you&#39;re new to Microsoft R Open, here are some <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/getting-started/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/getting-started/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ROxATCo0q-NyPassRgLU-\"><span>tips to get started,</span></a> and there are many <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/data/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/data/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DmswLsWPW7r4KeyfwYnBq\"><span>data sources you can explore with MRO</span></a>. Thanks go as always to the<a href=\"https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/what-is-r/#contributors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/what-is-r/%23contributors&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17LZvM5pY0hzWVIsueQDCN\"><span> contributors to the R Project</span></a> upon which RRO is built.</span></p>\r\n<p><span></span><br></p>\r\n<p><span>MRAN: <a href=\"https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/download/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/download/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241468548000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LSgHMo7PWv-kwNEq01Khr\"><span>Download Microsoft R Open</span></a></span></p>\r\n<p><span></span><br></p>\r\n<p><span>Regards,</span></p>\r\n<p><span>— Josée</span></p></div>"
    ]
